# Canonical commit identities.
#
# Commits made inside the dev container before the GIT_AUTHOR_* passthrough
# landed in docker-compose.yml (2026-04-22) went out with placeholder
# identities. The worst case is `dev@example.com`: GitHub matches commits to
# accounts by email, and an unrelated account owns that address, so 36 commits
# from 2026-02-08..02-23 are credited to a stranger on the contributor graph.
#
# This file fixes attribution for git's own tooling (log, shortlog, blame,
# `git log --author`). GitHub's contributor graph does NOT read .mailmap —
# only rewriting history would change the website, which is not worth a
# force-push on a public repo with forks. Set GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL
# in .env so it cannot recur.
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>

TurtleWolfe <TurtleWolfe@users.noreply.github.com> <dev@example.com>
TurtleWolfe <TurtleWolfe@users.noreply.github.com> <tortoisewolfe@example.com>
TurtleWolfe <TurtleWolfe@users.noreply.github.com> <101219421+TortoiseWolfe@users.noreply.github.com>
TurtleWolfe <TurtleWolfe@users.noreply.github.com> <turtlewolfe@users.noreply.github.com>
TurtleWolfe <TurtleWolfe@users.noreply.github.com> <SpokeToWork@gmail.com>
